              "text": "کھپانا — khapānā — \"to use up (time or effort); to toil over\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "اس نے اس کام میں دو سال کھپائے۔ us ne is kām meṅ do sāl khapāe. He spent two whole years toiling over this work."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past, with نے (he or she …): اس نے کام میں تین گھنٹے کھپائے, us ne kām meṅ tīn ghanṭe khapāe."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "کھپانا (khapānā) is inherited: CDIAL lists the Hindi cousin khapānā, \"to destroy\", under Sanskrit kṣapyatē, \"is destroyed, is used up\" (CDIAL 3655); CDIAL glosses it \"to destroy\", and the everyday sense \"to use up time or effort\" is a later one it does not record."
            }
          ]
        },
